WEBVTT

00:00:13.291 --> 00:00:15.991
I'm gonna go check in with Wade,
see if he knows what's going on.

00:00:16.131 --> 00:00:18.591
You're gonna see Wade
in that glass thing?

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:20.331
What is it, a teleportation box?

00:00:22.392 --> 00:00:24.432
It's a pay phone.
It's mostly for drug dealers

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:26.732
and fugitives from the law,
which is us.

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:28.971
Stay in the car.
I don't want anybody
seeing you.

00:00:29.131 --> 00:00:30.131
[groans] Fine.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.680
[makes driving noises]

00:00:38.224 --> 00:00:40.658
[motorcycles rumbling]

00:00:40.762 --> 00:00:41.762
Huh?

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:44.507
["All Fired Up"
by The Lazys plays]

00:00:48.216 --> 00:00:49.714
[gasps]

00:00:49.822 --> 00:00:52.222
Okay, okay.
That is the coolest
place on Earth,

00:00:52.342 --> 00:00:53.842
but you have to stay in the car.

00:00:55.485 --> 00:00:56.780
[indistinct chatter]

00:00:56.885 --> 00:00:58.424
[cheering]

00:00:58.529 --> 00:01:00.139
[panting]

00:01:01.468 --> 00:01:03.427
[revving]

00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:05.712
Be strong. Be strong.

00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:10.043
Hmm.

00:01:10.827 --> 00:01:13.068
[line ringing]

00:01:13.181 --> 00:01:15.041
Hello.
Green Hills Police Department.

00:01:15.482 --> 00:01:16.801
Wade, it's me.
Hi.

00:01:17.142 --> 00:01:18.301
I'm so glad that you called.

00:01:18.661 --> 00:01:21.141
Uh, so, some guys came in
asking some questions.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.641
Uh, they're a little creepy.

00:01:23.181 --> 00:01:25.781
Kind of reminded me of
the guys from Men in Black,

00:01:25.861 --> 00:01:29.001
but not as likable
or charming as Will Smith.

00:01:29.361 --> 00:01:30.361
Wait, what kind of questions?

00:01:30.841 --> 00:01:33.201
Um, questions about terrorism?
[nervous chuckle]

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:36.982
I told them that I've gone
ice fishing with Tom.

00:01:37.261 --> 00:01:38.661
He doesn't know how
to make a bomb.

00:01:38.881 --> 00:01:41.181
He can't even
make bait in the cold.

00:01:41.281 --> 00:01:42.982
All right, Wade, listen to me.
This is really important.

00:01:42.982 --> 00:01:44.801
Don't tell them
that we talked, okay?

00:01:47.931 --> 00:01:50.212
You know, I think
they already know.

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:53.511
Mr. Wachowski.
[groans]

00:01:55.271 --> 00:01:56.271
Tom.

00:01:56.431 --> 00:01:58.131
I want you to know
that the only other person

00:01:58.131 --> 00:02:00.712
who ever punched me in the face
was the school bully.

00:02:01.611 --> 00:02:04.351
He hit me in the cafeteria,
causing a blunt-force contusion

00:02:04.351 --> 00:02:06.671
to the soft tissue
surrounding my orbital bone.

00:02:07.311 --> 00:02:09.051
Humiliated me in front of
the entire school!

00:02:09.111 --> 00:02:10.451
And do you know
what I did in response?

00:02:11.271 --> 00:02:14.031
Uh, I'm assuming
that you reported him
to the principal's office

00:02:14.031 --> 00:02:15.931
'cause that kind of behavior
is really unacceptable.

00:02:15.932 --> 00:02:19.432
No. I examined
the inefficiency of a world
where brawn trumped brain

00:02:19.551 --> 00:02:21.932
and I used technology
to resolve that inefficiency.

00:02:22.391 --> 00:02:25.151
The boy ate his meals
through a straw for a year.

00:02:25.431 --> 00:02:27.371
And I have never
lost a fight again.

00:02:28.011 --> 00:02:29.011
Until today.

00:02:29.151 --> 00:02:30.611
Hey, hooray for me then, huh?

00:02:30.671 --> 00:02:32.951
No, because you're
about to become
the bully with the straw!

00:02:33.651 --> 00:02:35.331
I'm coming for you,
Mr. Wachowski.

00:02:36.151 --> 00:02:38.451
And when I catch you, I'll--

00:02:38.931 --> 00:02:39.931
[hangs up]
Hello.

00:02:40.232 --> 00:02:41.232
Hello?

00:02:42.111 --> 00:02:43.111
Hello, hello, hello?

00:02:43.111 --> 00:02:44.871
I think he actually hung up,

00:02:44.871 --> 00:02:46.692
because I notice
that the light isn't on.

00:02:46.732 --> 00:02:47.811
Thank you, Officer Brainfart.

00:02:48.192 --> 00:02:50.371
If you give me a second,
I can get an outside line.

00:02:50.451 --> 00:02:52.232
No. Don't be bothered.

00:02:52.712 --> 00:02:54.631
You just sit there and be "u"...

00:02:55.415 --> 00:02:57.020
...'seless.

00:03:04.081 --> 00:03:06.862
No one's gonna
erase my memory here?

00:03:07.982 --> 00:03:09.982
I will tell people about this!

00:03:10.115 --> 00:03:13.169
[rock music continues next door]

00:03:13.302 --> 00:03:17.782
Okay, not exactly
the healthiest meal, but...

00:03:17.782 --> 00:03:18.782
Sonic?

00:03:18.889 --> 00:03:20.860
[motorcycle rumbling]

00:03:22.974 --> 00:03:24.515
Oh, no.

00:03:25.089 --> 00:03:26.846
No, no, no, no, no!

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:30.931
["White Lightning" by
Tennessee River Crooks plays]

00:03:31.504 --> 00:03:33.476
Whoo!
Yeah!

00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:35.160
[whistling]

00:03:39.962 --> 00:03:42.112
[Tom clears throat]

00:03:42.221 --> 00:03:43.221
Howdy, pardner!

00:03:43.221 --> 00:03:44.541
I'm not your partner.
Come on. We're leaving.

00:03:44.761 --> 00:03:46.301
But there's a ZZ Top cover band.

00:03:46.382 --> 00:03:47.641
You gotta see their beards.

00:03:47.761 --> 00:03:50.101
You're gonna have to
catch 'em some other time.
Let's go. Get up!

00:03:50.101 --> 00:03:53.061
If we stay, I won't say another
word for the rest of the trip,

00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:54.942
starting... now.

00:03:56.022 --> 00:03:58.122
Welcome to the Piston Pit.
What can I get you fellas?

00:03:58.442 --> 00:04:00.662
I want nachos and buffalo wings,
oh, and guac.

00:04:00.821 --> 00:04:03.281
Funny word, isn't it?
Guac, guac! Guac.

00:04:03.402 --> 00:04:04.962
Hey, no kids
allowed in here.

00:04:05.241 --> 00:04:06.641
What's he got on,
some kind of mask?

00:04:06.662 --> 00:04:09.862
Oh, he's actually
43 years old and, um,

00:04:10.222 --> 00:04:12.081
suffers from
a very rare skin disease

00:04:12.081 --> 00:04:16.141
that stunts his growth
and makes him look, uh,
like that.

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:17.721
The face,
I was born with.

00:04:17.781 --> 00:04:20.281
The confidence,
I picked up along the way.

00:04:20.381 --> 00:04:23.273
Make his a Mello Yello, please.
Okay.

00:04:24.181 --> 00:04:26.982
You owe me one.
I never sat
on a barstool before.

00:04:27.261 --> 00:04:28.541
So squishy!

00:04:28.821 --> 00:04:30.321
Oh, look at this.
It spins.

00:04:30.962 --> 00:04:32.382
Yes.
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.244
That's nice.
I feel sick.

00:04:34.342 --> 00:04:35.342
Are you having fun?

00:04:35.601 --> 00:04:37.241
Gonna check this off
the ol' bucket list, huh?

00:04:37.301 --> 00:04:39.321
Big night for you.
What's a bucket list?

00:04:39.462 --> 00:04:41.942
[groans]
A bucket list is, uh...

00:04:42.442 --> 00:04:44.321
It's a list of things
you want to do in your life

00:04:45.002 --> 00:04:47.362
before you, well,
kick the bucket.

00:04:47.542 --> 00:04:49.042
I've never
kicked a bucket, either!

00:04:49.301 --> 00:04:50.541
Oh, I gotta make my list.

00:04:53.912 --> 00:04:54.912
Uh-huh. Mm-hmm.

00:04:55.352 --> 00:04:56.912
[chuckles] Oh, Sonic!

00:04:58.991 --> 00:04:59.991
Uh-huh.

00:05:04.581 --> 00:05:05.581
What? What's the matter?

00:05:05.761 --> 00:05:07.581
There's so much stuff
I've never done.

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.522
And now that I'm
leaving Earth forever,

00:05:10.622 --> 00:05:12.082
I guess I missed my chance.

00:05:18.212 --> 00:05:19.972
Well, I guess
this is the kind of place

00:05:19.972 --> 00:05:22.352
you could get a lot of living
done in a short period of time.

00:05:22.571 --> 00:05:24.872
I suppose we can spare an hour.

00:05:25.511 --> 00:05:27.531
What? You're gonna
bucket-list with me?

00:05:28.092 --> 00:05:30.551
Sure, why not?
You won't regret this.

00:05:30.712 --> 00:05:31.732
Oh, I'm pretty sure I will.

00:05:31.839 --> 00:05:34.511
["Bad News"
by Ghost Hounds plays]

00:05:54.569 --> 00:05:56.528
[dinging]

00:05:56.635 --> 00:05:58.666
[chuckles] New high score!

00:06:01.088 --> 00:06:02.798
Yippee-ki-yay!

00:06:03.297 --> 00:06:04.473
Ah-ha!

00:06:04.581 --> 00:06:06.142
Wait a second,
is this bull missing a head

00:06:06.222 --> 00:06:07.642
or does it have two butts?

00:06:10.222 --> 00:06:11.262
[laughing] This is easy.

00:06:11.372 --> 00:06:14.388
Okay.
Ha-ha! Yeehaw!

00:06:14.902 --> 00:06:17.146
[yelling]

00:06:17.256 --> 00:06:18.911
I'm a cowboy, baby!

00:06:19.536 --> 00:06:21.706
[yells]
[crashing]

00:06:22.331 --> 00:06:23.331
I'm okay.

00:06:24.566 --> 00:06:25.682
[Sonic laughing]
Whoo!

00:06:25.837 --> 00:06:26.837
Whoo! Yeah!

00:06:26.951 --> 00:06:27.951
[woman growls]
Ha-ha-ha!

00:06:32.722 --> 00:06:35.021
Yeah, yeah, laugh it up.

00:06:35.342 --> 00:06:36.642
[chuckles]
Nice work, Romeo.

00:06:37.242 --> 00:06:38.561
[sarcastic laugh]
Glad you're having a good time.

00:06:38.702 --> 00:06:40.182
I am having a good time!

00:06:40.242 --> 00:06:43.021
I'm having the best time.
I mean, what could go wrong?

00:06:45.202 --> 00:06:46.022
Uh...
[chuckles]

00:06:46.022 --> 00:06:47.702
Can we help you?

00:06:48.561 --> 00:06:50.242
We don't like
your kind around here.

00:06:50.442 --> 00:06:52.442
Our kind?
What kind is that?

00:06:55.202 --> 00:06:56.202
Hipsters.

00:06:56.382 --> 00:06:58.402
[gasps] How dare you.
Oh, hey. You know what?

00:06:58.402 --> 00:06:59.722
We were leaving anyway.
Weren't we?

00:06:59.822 --> 00:07:01.922
There's not a problem here.
No, no, no, it's okay.

00:07:01.922 --> 00:07:02.922
No, no, no,
we're leaving.

00:07:02.982 --> 00:07:05.422
I know exactly
how to handle this situation.

00:07:06.862 --> 00:07:07.962
[clears throat]
Pop quiz, hotshot.

00:07:08.322 --> 00:07:10.842
You just picked a fight with
a poorly disguised hedgehog

00:07:10.842 --> 00:07:12.782
who's seen way too many
action movies.

00:07:13.021 --> 00:07:15.342
What do you do? What do you do?

00:07:15.342 --> 00:07:16.322
[grunts]
[hollow thud]

00:07:16.322 --> 00:07:19.782
Huh. Am I crazy?
It's supposed to break, right?

00:07:21.622 --> 00:07:23.342
Dink! Dink-dink!
Break, please. Break, please.

00:07:23.442 --> 00:07:24.442
Break this bottle, please.
[growling]

00:07:24.482 --> 00:07:25.502
Please, please, please.
Uh, Sonic?

00:07:25.655 --> 00:07:26.655
[growls]

00:07:26.702 --> 00:07:27.437
Uh-oh!
[grunts]

00:07:27.437 --> 00:07:29.373
[men grunt]
[glass breaks]

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:32.667
[grunting]

00:07:36.539 --> 00:07:39.134
[Sonic] Oh-ho-ho-ho!
Nice going!

00:07:39.251 --> 00:07:40.692
Thanks! It's awesome right?

00:07:41.091 --> 00:07:42.631
All right, who's next?
Who wants some?

00:07:42.872 --> 00:07:44.292
Who do I get to beat up?

00:07:45.192 --> 00:07:47.131
Hey! Has anybody
seen my waitress?

00:07:47.212 --> 00:07:48.911
Still waiting on
those buffalo wings.

00:07:50.511 --> 00:07:51.511
[growling]
Why, you!

00:07:55.841 --> 00:07:58.384
Ha-ha-ha!
[blows]

00:08:00.361 --> 00:08:01.361
[growls]
Uh-oh!

00:08:01.438 --> 00:08:03.078
[growling]

00:08:03.442 --> 00:08:04.442
Really?

00:08:07.896 --> 00:08:10.233
["Boom" by
X Ambassadors plays]

00:08:15.815 --> 00:08:17.491
[glass tinkles]

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.026
[shutter clicks]

